course: dictionary
lesson: 7533
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Prayer» is a noun with three meanings: words said to God or a god, the act of praying, and, in the phrase «not have a prayer», no chance at all. Read the words around it to choose the right one.
explain: «Prayer can include thanks, saying sorry, asking for others and asking for ourselves.» Here prayer means the words people say to God, because the sentence lists what those words can contain. The clue comes after the word, in the list.
explain: «If a family says grace (a short prayer of thanks) before eating, you wait quietly until they finish.» The brackets give the meaning straight away. Brackets, commas and colons often explain a hard word for you.
explain: «A mosque is the Muslim place of prayer» tells you a mosque is where Muslims pray. Many faiths use prayer, and prayers can be said aloud, sung, or thought silently, at home, at school or in a place of worship.
fact: A prayer is words said to God or a god, to thank, praise or ask for help.
fact: Prayer is the act of praying.
fact: «Not have a prayer» means to have no chance at all.
fact: Many faiths use prayer, including Christians, Muslims, Jews, Hindus and Sikhs.
fact: Prayers can be said aloud, sung, or thought silently.
exercise: «If a family says grace (a short prayer of thanks) before eating, you wait quietly until they finish.» What is grace? | A place of worship | A dinner plate | *A short prayer of thanks | A quick game before lunch
exercise: Where do Muslims pray side by side in rows facing Mecca? | A football stadium | A market | *A mosque | A library
exercise: Jayden says, «Our team does not have a prayer of winning.» What does not have a prayer mean? | Lots of praying before the match | *No chance at all | Very good luck | Words said to a god
test: «Standing shoulder to shoulder shows that everyone is equal before God.» What does shoulder to shoulder mean here? | *Standing close together, side by side | Standing far apart | Turning your back on each other | Facing the wrong way
test: «Churches differ in leaders, baptism, style of worship, use of images and how they read the Bible, but all share belief in one God.» What do all churches share? | The same way of reading the Bible | The same leaders | The same images in every church | *Belief in one God
exam: Read «Prayers can be said aloud, sung, or thought silently.» Which statement is true? | Prayers can only be sung | Prayers can only be said aloud | *Prayers can be said aloud, sung or thought silently | Prayers are never said at school
